      },
      {
       "end_index": 5585,
       "start_index": 5485,
       "title": "Beschikking van 20/07/2023 ordonnantie betreffende het inburgerings- en begeleidingstraject voor nieuwkomers en buitenlandse personen",
       "type": "url_citation",
       "url": "https://etaamb.openjustice.be/nl/beschikking-van-20-juli-2023_n2023044135"
      },
      {
       "end_index": 5853,
       "start_index": 5732,
       "title": "Integration programme in Brussels: what are your obligations? - Commissioner Brussels Europe & International",
       "type": "url_citation",
       "url": "https://www.commissioner.brussels/integration-programme-in-brussels-what-are-your-obligations/"
      }
     ],
     "text": "**Short answer: yes — on the facts you give, the Brussels integration/welcome programme is mandatory for you**, unless you fall under a specific exemption.\n\n## 1) Is it mandatory? Exemptions?\n\nBecause you are **40**, a **non-EU / third-country national**, registering **for the first time** in the **foreigners’ register of a Brussels municipality**, with a **residence permit valid for more than 3 months**, and you have lived legally in Belgium for **less than 3 years**, you match the mandatory target group. The obligation has applied in Brussels since **1 June 2022**. ([newcomersin.brussels](https://www.newcomersin.brussels/en/target))\n\nRelevant exemptions include, in particular:\n\n- **EU/EEA/Swiss nationals** and certain equivalent categories;\n- certain **family members of EU/EEA/Swiss citizens**;\n- people who already obtained a recognised **integration/civic-integration certificate** or completed/obtained an equivalent recognised pathway;\n- people previously exempted from integration in another Belgian language area;\n- certain long-term residents of another EU Member State who already satisfied integration conditions there;\n- people with a Belgian recognised school diploma/certificate;\n- people with a serious illness or disability that permanently prevents participation;\n- certain temporary-stay situations. ([commissioner.brussels](https://www.commissioner.brussels/integration-programme-in-brussels-what-are-your-obligations/))\n\nSo: **mandatory unless your municipality/authority recognises that one of the exemptions applies to you.**\n\n## 2) Which authority or office should you contact?\n\nFirst, your **Brussels municipality** assesses whether you are subject to the obligation when you register in the foreigners’ register. If you are subject to it, the municipality gives you an **information brochure** and an **attestation/certificate of obligation**. ([newcomersin.brussels](https://www.newcomersin.brussels/en/trajectory))\n\nThen you must register with one of the recognised reception/integration offices:\n\n**Dutch-language pathway**\n- **BON** — Brussels, Schaerbeek or Anderlecht; Vivalis lists BON’s phone as **02 701 73 80**. ([vivalis.brussels](https://www.vivalis.brussels/fr/piloter-la-sante-et-le-social-a-bruxelles/quelles-sont-les-politiques-sociales-sante-que-nous/aide-aux-personnes/lintegration-des-primo-arrivants?utm_source=openai))\n\n**French-language pathway**\n- **BAPA BXL** — Brussels; **02 279 49 70**\n- **BAPA Convivial** — Forest **02 315 39 00** / Anderlecht **02 315 40 50**\n- **BAPA VIA** — Schaerbeek **02 563 52 50** / Molenbeek **02 563 52 51** ([vivalis.brussels](https://www.vivalis.brussels/fr/piloter-la-sante-et-le-social-a-bruxelles/quelles-sont-les-politiques-sociales-sante-que-nous/aide-aux-personnes/lintegration-des-primo-arrivants?utm_source=openai))\n\nVivalis is the Brussels Cocom/GGC administration responsible for the Brussels newcomers integration policy; since 2024, it manages the organisation of the BAPA pathways. ([vivalis.brussels](https://www.vivalis.brussels/nl/inburgeringstraject?utm_source=openai))\n\n## 3) Registration and completion deadlines\n\nAfter you receive your **residence card/permit** and the **certificate of obligation**, you have:\n\n- **6 months to register** with **BON or a BAPA**;\n- once registered, **18 months to complete** the programme. ([newcomersin.brussels](https://www.newcomersin.brussels/en/trajectory))\n\nYou must also ensure the municipality receives the **certificate of registration** and later the **certificate of completion**; this can be done via BON/BAPA, in person at the municipality, or by email according to the instructions on the certificate of obligation. ([newcomersin.brussels](https://www.newcomersin.brussels/en/trajectory))\n\nMissing deadlines can lead to an **administrative fine**, officially stated as ranging from **€100 to €2,500**. ([vivalis.brussels](https://www.vivalis.brussels/fr/piloter-la-sante-et-le-social-a-bruxelles/quelles-sont-les-politiques-sociales-sante-que-nous/aide-aux-personnes/lintegration-des-primo-arrivants?utm_source=openai))\n\n## 4) May you choose a French- or Dutch-language pathway?\n\n**Yes.** In Brussels you may choose either:\n\n- a **French-language pathway** with a **BAPA**, or\n- a **Dutch-language pathway** with **BON**.\n\nThe programme includes language learning where needed — **French or Dutch** depending on the chosen pathway/organisation. ([commissioner.brussels](https://www.commissioner.brussels/integration-programme-in-brussels-what-are-your-obligations/))\n\n## 5) Current official sources supporting this\n\nThe main official/current sources are:\n\n- **Vivalis — “L’intégration des primo-arrivants” / “Inburgering van nieuwkomers”**, setting out who is obliged, the offices, deadlines, suspension, and fine. ([vivalis.brussels](https://www.vivalis.brussels/fr/piloter-la-sante-et-le-social-a-bruxelles/quelles-sont-les-politiques-sociales-sante-que-nous/aide-aux-personnes/lintegration-des-primo-arrivants?utm_source=openai))\n- **Newcomers in Brussels — official Brussels information site**, especially “Target group” and “Programme steps,” explaining the conditions, exemptions link, municipality role, 6-month and 18-month deadlines. ([newcomersin.brussels](https://www.newcomersin.brussels/en/target))\n- **Ordinance of 20 July 2023** on the welcome/integration and support pathway for newcomers and foreign persons, published in the Belgian official legal database, defining the obliged “newcomer” and exemptions. ([etaamb.openjustice.be](https://etaamb.openjustice.be/nl/beschikking-van-20-juli-2023_n2023044135))\n- **Commissioner Brussels Europe & International / Expat Welcome Desk**, summarising Brussels obligations and listing the BAPA and BON operators. ([commissioner.brussels](https://www.commissioner.brussels/integration-programme-in-brussels-what-are-your-obligations/))",
